sections.text:
All hail the power of
Jesus' name
Let angels prostrate fall;
Let angels prostrate fall;
Bring forth the royal diadem
To crown Him Lord of all.

Jesus, the name that charms our fears;
That bids our sorrows cease;
'Tis music in the sinner's ears;
'Tis life, and health, and peace.

Odi, ẹ kọrin iyin Rẹ;
Aditi, gbohùn Rẹ;
Afojú, Olùgbàla de,
Ayarọ, fo f'ayọ!

Praise Him for His grace and favour
To our fathers in distress;
Praise Him, still the same forever;
Slow to chide, and swift to bless:
Praise Him, praise Him,
Glorious in His faithfulness.

Father-like He tends and spares us;
Well our feeble frame He knows,
In His hands He gently bears us,
Rescues us from all our foes;
Praise Him, praise Him,
Widely as His mercy flows.

For why? The Lord our God is good;
His mercy is for ever sure;
His truth at all times firmly stood.
And shall from age to age endure. Amen.

Olori ijọ t'ọrun
Layo l'a wole fun Ọ.
Ki Ọ to de, ijọ t'aye;
Y'o maa kọrin bíi t'ọrun;
A gbe ọkan wa s'oke,
Ni 'reti t'o ni 'bukun;
Awa kigbe, awa f'iyin
F'Ọlọrun igbala wa.

Be joyful, for He is the Lord,
On earth and in heaven supreme;
He fashions and rules by His word;
The “Mighty” and “Strong” to redeem.

Come, ye thankful people, come,
Raise the song of harvest home;
All is safely gathered in.
Ere the winter storms begin;
God our Maker doth provide,
For our wants to be supplied;
Come to God's own temple, come,
Raise the song of harvest home!

For the Lord our God shall come,
And shall take His harvest home;
From His field shall in that day
All offences purge away;
Give His angels charge at last,
In the fire the tares to cast;
But the fruitful ears to store,
In His garner evermore.

Then, thou church triumphant,
come,
Raise the song of harvest home;
All are safely gathered in,
Free from sorrow, free from sin;
There forever purified,
In God's garner to abide;
Come, ten thousand angels, come,
Raise the glorious harvest home!
Amen.

We are never, never weary
Of the grand old song;
Glory to God, Hallelujah;
We can sing it loud as ever,
With our faith more strong,
Glory to God, Hallelujah.

His love and His mercy
Surround me,
His grace like a river doth flow;
His Spirit, to guide and to
Comfort;
Is with me wherever I go.

Fún àánú t'ó pọ bíi yanrìn,
Tí mo ń gbà lojúmọ;
Lat'ọdọ Jésù Olúwa;
Kí l'èmi ó fi fún Un?

Èyí l'ohun t'èmi ó se;
F'ohun t'Ó se fún mi;
Èm' ó mú aago ìgbàlà;
N ó ké pe Ọlọrun.

Èyí l'ọpẹ tí mo lè dá,
Èmi òsì, àre;
Èm'ó máa sọrọ ẹbùn Rẹ;
N ó sì náa bèèrè sí i.

Èmi kò lè sì-ín b'ó ti tọ,
N kò ní'sẹ kan tó pé;
Sùgbọn èm'ó sògo yìí pé;
Gìbèsè ọpẹ mi pọ.
Ààmín.

Ohun t'á bùn Ọ, Olúwa,
'Wọ ó sàn-án lé padà fún wa;
L'áyo l'a ó ta Ọ l'ọrẹ;
Oníbú ọrẹ!.

Oh tell of His might ,
Oh sing of His grace,
Whose robe is the light;
Whose canopy space;
His chariots of wrath the deep
Thunder-clouds form;
And dark is His path on the
Wings of the storm.

O measureless Might,
Ineffable Love;
While angels delight to hymn
Thee above;
Thy humbler creation, though
Feeble their lays;
With true adoration shall sing to
Thy praise.
Amen.

Ẹ wolẹ f'Ọba ologo julọ,
Ẹ kọrin ipá àti ìfẹ Rẹ;
Aláàbò wa ni, àt'Ẹni ìgbàanì;
O ń gbé'nú ogo, Ẹlẹrù ní ìyìn.

Ẹ sọ ti 'pá Rẹ, ẹ sọ t'oore Rẹ;
'Mọlẹ l'asọ Rẹ, gọbì Rẹ, ọrun;
Àrá tí ń sán ni kẹkẹ 'bínú
Rẹ ję;
Ipa ọna Rẹ ni a kò sì lè mọ.

Ẹnu hà lè sọ ti ìtọjú Rẹ,
Nínú afẹfẹ, nínú ìmọlẹ;
Ìtọjú Rẹ wà nín'odò tí ó ń sàn;
O sì wà ninu ìrì àti òjò.

King of glory, King of Peace,
I will love Thee,
And that love may not cease,
I will love Thee;
Thou hast granted my request,
Thou hast heard me;
Thou didst note
My working breast;
Thou hast spared me.

Wherefore, with my utmost art,
I will sing Thee;
And the cream of all my heart,
I will bring Thee;
Though my sins against
Me cried,
Thou didst clear me;
And alone, when they replied,
Thou didst hear me.

Seven whole days,
Not one in seven;
I will praise Thee;
In my heart, though
Not in heaven,
I can raise Thee;
Small it is in this poor sort;
To enroll Thee;
E'en eternity is too short,
To extol Thee. Amen.

Ọba ògo, àlàáfíà,
Ń ó fẹràn Rẹ;
Ìfẹ náà kì yóó dẹkun;
Ń ó sún mọ Ọ;
Ńtorí Ó ti gbẹbẹ mi;
O ti gbóhùn mi;
O ka iwé àyà mi,
O dá mi ńdè.

Fún ìdásílẹ yìí ni,
Ń ó kọrin Rẹ;
Gbogb' ayọ ọkàn mi ni,
Ń ó mú fún Ọ;
'Gbà t'ẹsẹ mi ń ké kíkan;
O dá mi láre,
'Gbà mo pè Ọ ní 'kọkọ,
O gbẹbẹ mi.

Ẹ dé E l'ádé púpọ,
Ọd'àgùntàn Baba;
Gbọ bí orin ọrun ti bo
Orin gbogbo mọlẹ;
Jí, ọkàn mi, kọrin
T'ẹni t'ó kú fún ọ,
Se E l'Ọba rẹ t'ó ga jùlọ;
Títí, àni títí láéláé.

Se É l'Ọba àlàáfíà!
'Jọba Rẹ k'yó lópin,
Ní'bi tí ogun wolẹ fún Un;
Ìfẹ àti ìyin,
Àti yíká ẹṣẹ
Rẹ tí a kàn ní 'ṣòó;
Ẹgbẹrun èdè ní 'dàpọ;
Yó kọrin dídùn sí I.

Se Olúwa 'Ọba
Tí ó gúnwà l'ókè;
Se É l'Ọba tí a gún l'ọkọ;
Ìyanu 'ti ìfẹ;
Ẹ dé E l'adé púpọ;
Àwọn tí ń gbé ayé:
Àti gbogbo ọba ayé,
Ń'torí Oun l'Ọba ẹdá.

Se É l'Ọba gbogbo 'gbà;
Ọba ayeraye;
Ẹlẹdàá gbogbo ìràwọ;
Àgbà 'yanu l'èyí;
Olùràpadà wa!
Tó kú nítorí mi;
Ìyin Rẹ kì yóó lópin láé,
Láéláé àti láéláé.
Ààmín.

Njẹ, bẹ ọkàn mi yìí wò
Lé òkùnkun ẹsẹ lọ;
F'ìmọlẹ ọrun kún mi;
Sì tú àìgbàgbọ mi ká;
Máà f'ara Rẹ hàn mí sí I,
Títí di ọjọ pipe. Ààmín.

Alelúyà! Ọba ọrun,
I-wọ ni Olu-wa wa;
Alelúya! Ọmọ Wundia
Tí ó gúnwà lórí ìtẹ;
A fún Ọ l'órúkọ gíga,
Olórí àlùfáà ńlá;
'Wọ ti fi ara Rẹ rúbọ;
Ẹbọ Ọlọrun dídùn. Àmín.

Grace taught my soul to pray,
And made mine eyes o'er flow;
'Tis grace has kept me
To this day;
And will not let me go.

Oore-ọfẹ ń kọ mi,
Bí a ti gbàdúrà;
Ó pa mi mọ títí d'óní;
Kò sì jẹ kí n sáko.

Jí, ọkàn mi, dìde l'áyo,
Kọrin ìyìn Olùgbàlà;
Ọlá Rẹ beere orin mi;
'Seun ìfẹ Rẹ ti pọ tó?

O ríi, mo sègbé ní 'subú,
Ṣíbẹ Ó fẹ mi l'á fẹ tán;
Ó yọ mí nínú òsì mi;
'Seun 'fẹ Rẹ ti tóbì tó!

Great Father of Glory,
Pure Father of Light,
Thine angels adore thee,
All veiling their sight;
All laud we would render;
O help us to see;
'Tis only the splendor of light
Hideth Thee. Amen.

Mímọ, Mímọ, Mímọ!
B'òkùnkùn pa Ọ mọ,
Bí ojú ẹlẹṣẹ kò lè rí ògo Rẹ;
Ìwọ nikan ló mọ,
kò tún s'ẹlòmíràn;
Pípé ń'nu agbára àti ní'fẹ.

We praise Thee o God,
For the Son of Thy love;
For Jesus who died;
And is now gone above.

Ọlọrun yíi tóbì l'Ọba,
J'àwọn òrìṣà lọ;
Gbogb'ayé wà ní'kaáwọ Rẹ;
Àt'àwọn òkè ńlá.

Lójooújúmọ títí ayé
Ni kí á máa kọrin;
K'á máa yọ nínú Olúwa;
Títí ayérayé.
Àmín.

Thou art a port protected
From storms that round us rise;
A garden intersected
With streams of Paradise;
Thou art a cooling fountain
In life's dry dreary sand;
From Thee, like Pisgah's
Mountain,
We view our promised land.

Èbùte ààbò ni Ọ,
Láàrin ìjì ayé;
Ọgbà dídára ni Ọ,
Ní 'b'omi ìyè ń sàn;
Orísun 'tura ni Ọ,
Láyé aginjù yìí;
L'órí Rẹ, bí ní Písgà
L'a ń wo 'lẹ ìlérí.

A fẹ ìsinmi t'ayé yìí,
Ṣùgbọn 'sinmi t'ọrun dùn jù;
Èyí nì l'ọkàn wa ń lépa;
Pẹlú ìtara òun ìfẹ.

Kò sí ìdágììrì ọtá,
Bẹẹ ni kò sí 'payà ní'bẹ;
Kò sí òru, kò sí 'kùukùu;
Àfí ọsán títí láéláé.

'Gbà náà n ó ri,
N ó gbọ, n ó mọ;
Ohun gbogbo tí mo ti ń fẹ;
Gbogbo ipa mi y'o dà pọ,
Láti se ìfẹ Rẹ títí.
Ààmín.

This is the day of light;
Let there be light today;
O day-spring, rise upon
Our night,
And chase its gloom away.

This is the day of peace;
Thy peace our spirits fill;
Bid Thou the blasts of
Discord cease,
The waves of strife be still.

Ọjọ àdúrà ni;
K'áyé sún mọ ọrun;
Gb'ọkàn wa s'ókè s'ọdọ Rẹ,
Sì pàdé wa níhìn-ín.

Ọba ọjọ l'èyí;
Fún wa ní ìṣojú;
Jí òkú ọkàn wa sí'fẹẹ
'Wọ aṣẹgun ikú.
Ààmín.

Ó pàṣẹ k'á bọwọ
Fún ọjọ ìsinmi;
Ìbínú Rẹ tóbì púpọ;
S'áwọn t'ó rúfin yìí.

Mo f'ọnà'ta àt'ẹkun rẹ;
Ilé t'á se l'ọṣọ,
Ilé t'á kọ fún Ọlọrun;
Láti fi àánú hàn.

Ayọ sì ni wákàtí náà,
Tí mo lò ń'nú àgbàlaá Rẹ;
Láti mọ adùn àdúrà;
Láti gba mánà ọrọ Rẹ.

Osẹ, Osẹ rere
Ìwọ ọjọ sinmi;
O yẹ k'á fi ọjọ kan,
Fún Ọlọrun rere;
B'ọjọ mí-ìn tilẹ m'ẹkun wá,
Ìwọ ń n' ojú wa nú;
Ìwọ tí s'ọjọ ayọ,
Emi fẹ dídé rẹ.

Jẹ k'ọmọ kékeré,
Lá àlá rere;
S'ọlọkọ t'éwu ń wu;
Ní ojú omi.

Father, breathe an evening blessing,
Ere repose our spirits seal;
Sin and want we come confessing;
Thou canst save, and Thou canst heal.
Though the night be dark and dreary,
Darkness cannot hide from Thee;
Thou art He, who never weary,
Watchest where Thy people be.

Hold Thou Thy Cross
Before my closing eyes;
Shine through the gloom,
And point me to the skies;
Heav'ns morning breaks,
And earth's vain shadows flee;
In life, in death, O Lord, abide
With me! Amen.

And some have found the world is vain,
Yet from the world they break not free;
And some have friends who give them pain,
Yet have not sought a friend in Thee;

O Saviour Christ, Thou too art Man;
Thou hast been troubled, tempted, tried;
Thy kind but searching glance can scan;
The very wounds that shame would hide.

Sages, leave your contemplations;
Brighter visions beam afar;
Seek the great Desire of nations,
Ye have seen His natal star.

Joy to the world! The Lord is come;
Let earth receive her King;
Let every heart prepare Him room,
And heaven and nature sing,
And heaven and nature sing
And heaven, and heaven and nature sing.

While shepherds watch'd their
flocks by night,
All seated on the ground;
The Angel of the Lord
Came down;
And glory shone around.

"To you in David's town,
this day,
Is born of David's line;
The Saviour who is Christ
the Lord;
And this shall be the sign."

All glory to God on high;
And to the earth be peace;
Goodwill henceforth from
heav'n to men
Begin and never cease.
Amen.

Bí àwọn Olùs'àgùntan
Ti ń s'agbo wọn l'oru;
Áńgẹl' Olúwa sọkalẹ;
Ògo ràn yí wọn ká.

Ààjìn jìn, oru mimọ,
'Mọlẹ dé, òòkùn sá;
Olùs'àgùntàn gb'orin ángẹlì;
“Kábíyèsí, Alelúyà Ọba,
Jésù Olùgbàlà dé,
Jésù Olùgbàlà dé”.

Ààjìn jìn, oru mimọ,
'Ràwọ ọrun tàn 'mọlẹ;
Wo àwọn Amòye ìlà oòrùn;
Mú ọrẹ wọn wá fún Ọba wa;
Jésù Olùgbàlà dé,
Jésù Olùgbàlà dé.

Once in royal David's city,
Stood a lowly cattle shed;
Where a mother laid her baby,
In a manger for His bed;
Mary was that mother mild,
Jesus Christ her little child.

And through all His wondrous childhood
He would honour and obey,
Love, and watch the lowly mother;
In whose gentle arms He lay;
Christian children all must be,
Mild, obedient, good as He.

And our eyes at last shall see Him,
Through His own redeeming love;
For that child, so dear and gentle,
Is our Lord in heaven above;
And He leads His children on;
To the place where He is gone.

Nígbà kan ní Bẹtlẹhẹmù,
Ilé kékéré kan wà,
Ní'bi ìyá kan tẹ'mọ rẹ sí,
Lórí ibùjẹ ẹran;
Màríà n'ìyá ọmọ náà;
Jésù Kríst' sì l'ọmọ náà.

A ó f'ojú wa rí I níkẹyìn,
Ní agbára ifẹ Rẹ;
Nítorí Ọmọ rere yíì,
Ni Olúwa wa l'ọrun;
O ń tọ àwa ọmọ Rẹ,
S'ọnà ibi tí Òun lọ.

And through all His wondrous childhood
He would honour and obey,
Love, and watch the lowly mother;
In whose gentle arms He lay;
Christian children all must be,
Mild, obedient, good as He.

And our eyes at last shall see Him,
Through His own redeeming love;
For that child, so dear and gentle,
Is our Lord in heaven above;
And He leads His children on;
To the place where He is gone.

Cold on His cradle the dew-drops are shining;
Low lies His head with beast of the stall,
Angels adore Him in slumber reclining;
Maker, and Monarch, And Saviour of all.

A ó f'ojú wa rí I níkẹyìn,
Ní agbára ifẹ Rẹ;
Nítorí Ọmọ rere yíi,
Ni Olúwa wa l'ọrun;
O ń tọ àwa ọmọ Rẹ,
S'ọnà ibi tí Òun lọ.

Ìwọ Ọrọ Ọlọrun
Ọgbọn àt'òkè wá,
Òótọ tí kìí yípadà,
Ìmọlẹ ayé wa;
Àwá yin Ọ fún 'mọlẹ
T'ínú ìwé Mímọ;
Fítìlà fún ẹsẹ wa;
Tí ń tán títí ayé.

Ìwọ Ọrọ Ọlọrun
Ọgbọn àt'òkè wá,
Òótọ tí kìí yípadà,
Ìmọlẹ ayé wa;
Àwá yin Ọ fún 'mọlẹ
T'ínú ìwé Mímọ;
Fítìlà fún ẹṣẹ wa;
Tí ń tàn títí ayé.

Master, speak Thy servant heareth,
Waiting for Thy gracious word,
Longing for Thy voice that cheereth;
Master, let it now be heard
I am listening, Lord, for Thee;
What hast Thou to say to me?

Master speak though least and lowest,
Let me not unheard depart;
Master, Speak for O Thou knowest
All the year-ning of my heart;
Knowest all its truest need;
Speak, and make me blest indeed.

Àsìírí Olódùmarè:
Ìkọ Ọba ọrun;
Ìdà tó pa oró ikú;
Àwòrán Ọlọrun.

Wá b'àwọn 'mọ Rẹ sọrọ
Tọ wọn s'ọna mímọ́;
Fí ayọ̀ kún ọkàn wọn,
Fí àdúrà kọ wọn;
Kí wọn f'ayé wọn rúbọ
Kí wọn f'ayé wọn jì;
K'ijọba Rẹ yára dé,
K'ojú wa lè rí Ọ.

A glory glides the sacred page,
Majestic, like the sun;
It gives a light to every age;
It gives, but borrows none.

The hand that gave it still
supplies,
The gracious light and heat;
His truths upon the nations rise;
They rise, but never set.

Just obey, just obey;
is the way; God's way;
When His message comes
To you,
There is but one thing to do
Just obey, just obey.

B'Ọlọrun Ọba ọrun
Ti máa ń sọrọ ní 'gbàa nì;
Ó tún ń bá wa sọrọ bẹẹ lónìí;
Arákùnrịn, òótọ ni
Ohun t' Ó bá wí fún ọ;
Ohun kan l'àigbọdọ-má-se,
gbọràn.

Whosoever cometh need not delay;
Now the door is open, enter while you may;
Jesus is the True and only Living Way:

“Whosoever will,” the promise is secure;
“Whosoever will,” forever shall endure;
“Whosoever will,” 'tis life for evermore. Amen.

From death unto life He hath brought us,
And made us by grace Sons of God;
A fountain is opened for sinners;
Oh, wash and be cleans'd in the blood.

Accept now God's offer of mercy;
To Jesus, oh, hasten today;
For He will receive him that cometh,
And never will turn him away.
Amen.

The Comforter has come!
The Comforter has come!
The Holy Ghost from heaven;
The Father's promise given;
Oh, spread the tidings round;
Wherever man is found;
The Comforter has come!

The mighty King of kings
With healing in His wings;
To every captive soul;
A full deliverance brings;
And through the vacant cells;
The song of triumph rings;
The Comforter has come!

Oh, boundless love divine;
How shall this tongue of mine;
To wandering mortals tell;
The matchless grace divine;
That I may with Him dwell;
And in His image shine;
The Comforter has come!

Oh, let the echoes fly;
Above the vaulted sky;
And all the saints above;
To all below reply;
In strain of endless love;
The song that ne'er will die;
The Comforter has come!
Amen.

Come, ye sinners, poor and wretched,
Come in mercy's gracious hour;
Jesus ready stands to save you,
Full of pity, love, and pow'r,
He is able;
He is willing, doubt no more.

Let not conscience make You linger,
Nor of fitness fondly dream;
All the fitness He requireth
Is to feel your need of Him:
This He gives you;
'Tis the Spirit's rising beam.

Padà, asáko sí'le rẹ,
Jésù l'Ó sá ń pè ọ,wá
Ẹmí pẹlú Ìjọ sì ń pè;
Yára, sá àsàlà;
Padà, Padà.

Padà, asáko sí'le rẹ;
Wèrè ni b'ó bá pẹ,
K'ò sí dàríji ní'bojì;
Ọjọ àánú kúrú;
Padà, Padà. Ààmín.

Cease of fitness to be thinking;
Do not longer try to feel;
It is trusting, and not feeling
That will give the Spirit's seal.

Jésù ń dúró de 'pinnu rẹ
Se ìpinnu fún Un lónìí;
Nígbà tí Ẹmí Rẹ ń rọ ọ;
Wá s'ọdọ Olùgbàlà.

Jesus loves me and I know I love Him:
Love brought Him down my poor soul to redeem;
Yes, it was love made Him die on the tree;
Oh, I am certain that Jesus loves me!

Háà! Ọjọ iyanu, ọjọ 'yanu,
Ọjọ ti n ko le gbagbe;
'Gba mo sako lo ninu
okunkun,
Ni mo ba Jesu pade;
Ọrẹ, Olufe, Eni ikaanu
B'okan aini mi pade;
O mu beru lo, pẹl'ayo ni
mo ń royin,
O mu gbogbo okunkun lọ!

Agbára ... ńlá ...
Tí ń siṣẹ 'yanu;
Ń bẹ nínú ... Ẹjẹ Rẹ...
Agbára ... ńlá ...
Tí ń siṣẹ 'yanu;
Ńbẹ nínú Ẹjẹ Jésù.

Come to the Saviour, make no delay;
Here in His word He has shown us the way;
Here in our midst He's standing today
Tenderly saying, “Come!”

Jẹ k'àwọn 'mọdé wá
gb'óhùn Rẹ,
Jẹ k'ọkàn gbogbo
wa fò fún ayọ;
K'á sì yan Jésù l'àyànfẹ wa;
Má dúró, sùgbọn wá.

Gba ọrọ náà rò, Jésù ń dúró,
